# Exclude everything, then allow only what runtime/livetalking/Dockerfile copies.
# Docker applies the last matching rule, so the forbidden categories below the
# allow list also apply inside vendor/LiveTalking.
*
!vendor/LiveTalking/**
!runtime/patches/livetalking-*.patch
!runtime/patches/livetalking.series
!runtime/patches/LIVETALKING_MODIFICATIONS.md
!runtime/livetalking/launcher.py
!runtime/livetalking/shuzhiren_secrets.py
!runtime/livetalking/shuzhiren_aigc_label.py
!runtime/livetalking/shuzhiren_overlay.py
!runtime/livetalking/avatar_builder_api.py
!runtime/livetalking/avatar_publisher_api.py
**/.git
**/.git/**
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/secrets
**/secrets/**
**/weights
**/weights/**
**/recordings
**/recordings/**
**/exports
**/exports/**
**/cache
**/cache/**
**/logs
**/logs/**
**/*.log
# Model weights and avatar data are mounted read-only at deploy time. Only the
# LiveTalking root directories are excluded: avatars/*/models are Python packages.
vendor/LiveTalking/models
vendor/LiveTalking/models/**
vendor/LiveTalking/data
vendor/LiveTalking/data/**
